{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Plan-review gate EARNED (not bypassed); PS2's LLM-Review -1 remediated\n\nChange **2683 patchset 3**.\n\n### The blocking finding\n\n`(bugfix-size-attestation)` — 1187 non-test lines against a 150-line floor for a bug fix, with no\nacceptable plan-review attestation. Remedied by earning it.\n\n**Preconditions checked BEFORE spending a billed review**, since both are traps:\n- Description is **5,498 chars**, under the 8,000 admission cap — no shortening needed.\n- `file_impact` was **undeclared** while the change touches 14 files. Widening it is a MATERIAL\n  change that would stale an attestation, so it was set to all 14 paths with per-path reasons\n  **first**, then the review was run. Doing it in the other order would have invalidated the\n  attestation the gate demands.\n\n**Verdict: `PASS`, 0 blocking** (2 advisory, 1 coaching), `pydantic_ai` /\n`bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6`, 259.7 s, `source=attested` at\n`4c9940348148fb255b17ddf1cb124701ad4565d7`. Attestation **persisted and verified**:\n`rebar review-plan --status` → `certified`, and `rebar verify-signature --kind plan-review` →\n*\"certified — ssh-keygen -Y verify accepted signature\"*. One review run, no duplicate, **no\n`--force` and no bypass of any kind**.\n\n### The 8 advisories — every one was drift my own patchset 2 introduced\n\nThree were the exact failure this change argues against: a comment asserting a property the\nconfiguration no longer has.\n\n- `monitoring.tf:80` and `monitoring_9ea3.tf:74` — headers still read \"PROFILE A (dead-man), 3-of-3\n  over 15 minutes\" while the resources below were already `6`/`6` (30 min). Corrected. When I\n  widened those windows after the 20:47Z event I updated the reasoning paragraphs and missed the\n  one-line headers above them.\n- `observability.sh:1488` — the publisher-side §5 comment still described the alarm's \"2-of-3\n  five-minute window … two breaching datapoints inside 15 minutes\" after I rewindowed it to 8-of-8\n  / 40 min. Corrected minimally (3 lines). **Checked against change 2684 first**: that change's\n  nearest `observability.sh` hunks are at old lines 1495 and 1511, mine is 1486-1489, so there is\n  **no textual conflict** and no sequencing needed.\n- Invariant labels disagreed between the test docstring (I1 = M==N, I2 = 900 s window, I3 = 600 s\n  budget) and the runbook (which named the 600 s rule I2 and left the 900 s rule unnamed). Settled\n  on the test's numbering and made the runbook **and the commit message** match — the message had\n  the same defect and was not in the review's line-scope.\n\n### One advisory worth answering rather than just fixing\n\n`monitoring.tf:111` `(scope-intent)` flagged the `gerrit_gate_down` 10→30 min detection regression\nas an alarm \"the ticket never names\". Answered explicitly in the commit message rather than\nsilently: it fires on the **same** mechanism (`breaching` with `datapoints_to_alarm` below\n`evaluation_periods`), and it sat at 2-of-2 rather than the ticket's 2-of-3, which is exactly why\nthe ticket's eight-site survey missed it — it is strictly *more* exposed, not less. That was a\nnear-miss argument until 20:47Z, when it fired with *\"no datapoints were received for 2 periods and\n2 missing datapoints were treated as [Breaching]\"* while Gerrit answered in 0.266 s. Excluding it\nwould have left a proven instance of this ticket's own defect standing beside twenty-six fixed\nones.\n\n`terraform fmt -check` / `validate` clean, `bash -n` clean on the one-comment observability.sh\ntouch, 29 alarm tests pass, `check_orphaned_load.py` exit 0. Terraform remains **unapplied**.\nPatchset 3 pushed to the same Change-Id `I6da112c2…`; `LLM-Review` and `Verified` re-running. Not\nsubmitted."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788643297712156001,"uuid":"e4160f38-3fe8-4894-8a46-073ad4bd334d"}